<title>USA: FED ADDS RESERVES THORUGH OVERNIGHT SYSTEM RPS.</title>
<headline>FED ADDS RESERVES THORUGH OVERNIGHT SYSTEM RPS.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-08-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Federal Reserve added reserves into the banking system on Tuesday via overnight system repurchase agreements, the New York Fed confirmed.</p>
<p>The operation, which followed Monday's three-day system RPs, was generally expected.</p>
<p>Federal funds were trading at 5-9/16 percent, above the 5-1/2 percent target rate in morning trading.</p>
<p>(( -- N.A. Treasury Desk, 212-859-1867 ))</p>
